<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian grain supply/disposal estimates.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian grain supply/disposal estimates.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian Bureau of Agricultural and Resource Economics (ABARE) issued the following forecasts of the supply and disposal of Australian wheat, barley and sorghum for the 1996/97 growing season ending March 31, 1997. Based on data as at Feb 25, in million tonnes:</p>
<p>				   1996/97   1995/96     1994/95</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>    Production		  23.50     16.98	  8.90</p>
<p>    Domestic use		 3.51	4.12	  3.88</p>
<p>	Human and industrial   1.85	1.84	  1.83</p>
<p>	Feed			 1.18	1.78	  1.61</p>
<p>	Seed			 0.49	0.50	  0.44</p>
<p>    Net Exports		 16.00     12.75	  6.36</p>
<p>    Change in stocks	  +3.40     +0.11	 -1.34</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>    Production		   6.08	5.50	  2.79</p>
<p>    Domestic use		 2.20	2.02	  2.20</p>
<p>	Malt, other human use  0.15	0.22	  0.16</p>
<p>	Feed			 1.90	1.65	  1.90</p>
<p>	Seed			 0.14	0.15	  0.14</p>
<p>    Net Exports		  3.93	3.93	  1.49</p>
<p>	Feed barley		1.47	1.71	  0.52</p>
<p>	Malting barley	   1.96	1.83	  0.57</p>
<p>	Malt (grain equiv)     0.50	0.39	  0.40</p>
<p>SORGHUM</p>
<p>    Production		   0.99	1.56	  1.27</p>
<p>    Domestic use		 0.90	1.00	  1.22</p>
<p>	Feed			 0.90	1.00	  1.22</p>
<p>	Seed ('000 tonnes)	  3	   2	     3</p>
<p>    Net exports ('000 tonnes)  83	 553	    53</p>
<p>NOTE: Export estimates apply to marketing years of October-September for wheat, November-October for barley and March-February for sorghum. Figures are rounded.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373 1800</p>
</text>
